  "recommendation": {
    "word": "hold",
    "why": "The shipped flag keeps the panel layer at the final size on every morph frame, shows every child where the original shows it (Lean paint_eq, inset_width_eq) and passes the breakpoint gate on both engines. The measured counts belong to a first design with a wrapper element, which failed the gate; they show no difference from the base beyond the pass-to-pass spread, which is expected since layout inputs are unchanged, and the Simulator has no GPU and logs no surface allocations. The final design run 39760667274 (the 5th dispatch, 39751427150, hung and was cancelled) shows morph-open Composite per frame lower (100214-148161 us against 176345-180949 us, cells do not overlap) and the close push overlapping the base; resized layers per read do not fall (1250-1300 against 833-1250 per 100 reads), so the panel layer is not told apart by id and the saving is not shown. The nav resize and the column tracks still change size on every frame. Hold until a lane with a real GPU judges it."
  }
